WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0012: BG3's effects, spell previews and ground markers drawn with WoW's camera,
BG3's route line on WoW's ground
(on top of 0001-0009 and 0011; skip 0010).

- wowbg3_fx_render.rs: each WoW frame BG3's camera blocks in the replay arena (set 0 binding 2,
  the per-view block, and set 0 binding 1's camera axes) are rewritten with WoW's own camera mapped
  into BG3's coordinates (world mode's mapping, the ground lock added back). BG3 renders a cast
  through its action camera while WoW keeps the camera record's pose, so Fire Bolt's preparation
  and impact used to land off-screen or behind WoW's ground; the clearance dolly and BG3's frame
  lag no longer move the effects either. WoW's depth needs no eye shift then. `WOW_BG3_FX_CAMERA=bg3`
  keeps BG3's camera (the old way). Special key 6 (BG3's G-buffer normal, which projected decals
  read: spell areas, landing and target markers) is one texel per frame, WoW's ground taken as
  level in the camera's axes. G-buffer decal draws (four targets) are skipped with a note: those
  seen only darken BG3's albedo under the previews the effects pass draws.
- wowbg3_fx.rs: the camera blocks' blob offsets per frame (`find_cam_blocks`); the mapping from
  `tav.bin` (`bg3_map`, `WOW_BG3_LINK_DIR`); `strip_block` accepts BG3's current per-view block (V
  with the eye's translation, camera-relative VP), so the TAA jitter comes out again and the
  block's far plane (333 m, which the decals rebuild positions with) reaches the depth prep;
  missing files are looked for again after 150 ms instead of 2 s (a cast's textures arrive as it
  starts).
- wowbg3_route.rs (new, a child of wowbg3_fx): BG3's route line (turn-based mode, sneaking) on
  WoW's ground. BG3 draws it into an offscreen target of its own, as a tube at BG3's floor heights,
  so the capture layer sends its segments (`bg3route.bin`, "RTE1") instead of a draw to replay.
  Each segment is mapped into WoW (the ground lock taken off), cut into pieces and projected onto
  WoW's terrain and WMO faces (the selection ring's projector) with BG3's colours, width, dashes,
  gaps and end fades. Replaces the draft route from BG3's pathfinder (`PTH1`, `wowbg3_path.rs`),
  which drew a line wherever the cursor was, also where BG3 shows none.

